 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186124866 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x) = (x + \\frac{5}{6})^{2} - \\frac{1}{2}$?" 13194139536054 17592186045417 false] [17592186124866 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x)={(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}?$" 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186124866 1074 "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-\\frac{5}{6}$ and $k=-\\frac{1}{2},$ the vertex is $(-\\frac{5}{6},-\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ).$ \n\n![](images/54/54e0b0ea5dd498a36fc854781dc5120ce1de9bee0c333eecc6d895ce09b72424.png)" 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186124930 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186124930 1071 "What is the domain of the function $f(x) = (x + 6)^{2} - 6$?" 13194139536054 17592186045417 false] [17592186124930 1071 "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=(x+6)^{2}-6?$" 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186124930 1074 "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186125237 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186125237 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x) = 2x^{2} - 4x + 5$?" 13194139536054 17592186045417 false] [17592186125237 1071 "What is the range of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4x+5?$" 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186125237 1074 "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=2>0,$ $b=-4,$ and $c=5.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{(-4)}{2\\cdot 2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}-4x+5 \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-4(1)+5 \\\\  & =2-4+5 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(1,3),$ and the range of the function is $[3,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/a8/a8fc15df2b24054485bb07330f40919ebf13cb9969073a733b9426a28dab20b5.png)" 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186128946 1071 "![](images/0f/0f341a3893509e9adc2b5897e14a87656aa3c49824dda809ae6030646c6ece79.svg)\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PCP^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" 13194139536054 17592186045417 true] [17592186128946 1071 "![](images/d1/d1bc2b703c1d73e735bdbb1d2abab86f86447e87fbeabde57126114726f78757.png)\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PCP^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" 13194139536054 17592186045417 false] [17592186128946 1074 "Recall that for any $2 \\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PCP^{-1},$ where \n\n![](images/48/489a26b52ac132d82ffa918d931963a0cd33df092aea8e70885dc41c4e363be5.svg)\n\nand $\\mathbf{v}$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda.$\n\n- From the matrix ![](images/bf/bfc2be5324b72df4c3c63e92c4501bbda6b0fcde0ef8e6284d739db51e73a722.svg) we deduce that $\\textrm{Re}(\\lambda)={\\color{blue}3}$ and $\\textrm{Im}(\\lambda) = {\\color{red}-1}.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda = {\\color{blue}3}+({\\color{red}-1})\\text{i} = 3-\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix ![](images/1f/1fd5d191e88cd5f00ffd91f83800ce0c82024cedea60bf78432cd0abb504252a.svg) we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n![](images/df/df9978ae9ef1bb16b79e36abace84ef559ef64